commits.body:
TPdfEnum applied EMR_EXTSELECTCLIPRGN as q ... W n, but only the current DC state knew of it:
- after EMR_RESTOREDC the inner clip stayed in force;
- a clip selected after SaveDC, or one that SetMetaRgn made part of the meta region, left its q open, so the content stream had more q than Q;
- after the Q of a new clip, a line drawn with the same pen came out in the stroke colour, width and dash of before.

The regions are now kept as PDF boxes. Each DC state names its own region and the regions SetMetaRgn kept. SelectClip makes the canvas hold that clip; it runs from ExtSelectClipRgn, from RestoreDC, from PathEnded after a path is painted, and at the end of RenderMetaFile. After its Q it forgets the cached pen and fill values.

A clip changed between BeginPath and the painting of the path now waits for the painting record. PDF allows no q or Q within a path, and before, the q or Q of such a clip was written in the middle of the path. In the same case:
- ScaleMatrix no longer strokes the half-built path;
- EMR_SELECTCLIPPATH ends the path (its clip is still not applied);
- a path never painted is ended with the metafile;
- the next segment after a path starts with its own m.

GDI paints such a path under the new clip, the renderer under the one of before; fixing that needs the path buffered. Test EmfClipRestoreDC, 13 checks: 8 of them fail before. This is the same change as in our engine (martin-doyle/mORMot2-PDF-CrossPlatform#93).

